Third-party material in this repository
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

backend/docker/grobid/grobid.yaml
  Modified from the default configuration of GROBID
  (https://github.com/kermitt2/grobid), Apache License 2.0.

frontend/webui/src/components/Markdown.tsx (safeUrlTransform)
  Adapted from react-markdown's defaultUrlTransform
  (https://github.com/remarkjs/react-markdown), MIT License.

backend/benchmarks/munin_bench/faithfulness/minicheck.py
  Reimplements the inference procedure of MiniCheck
  (Tang et al. 2024, https://github.com/Liyan06/MiniCheck), MIT License.

LitQA2 / LAB-Bench (FutureHouse, https://huggingface.co/datasets/futurehouse/lab-bench)
  CC BY-SA 4.0. This repository commits only LitQA2 question identifiers and
  source DOIs, and per-question scores. The questions themselves are loaded
  from the dataset at run time and are not redistributed here.

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Software and models fetched at build or run time (not distributed here)
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Munin's Dockerfiles and compose files pull the components below when you
build or start the stack. Each stays under its own license. Munin uses them
unmodified, as separate programs, unless noted.

  Neo4j Community Edition          GPL-3.0     graph database (Bolt client only)
  SearXNG                          AGPL-3.0    metasearch; only our settings.yml is mounted
  Ghostscript, jbig2dec            AGPL-3.0    pulled in by ocrmypdf in the retrieval image
  TeX Live, biber                  LPPL / GPL / Artistic, mixed   sandbox image
  GROBID (incl. pdfalto)           Apache-2.0 (pdfalto GPL-2.0)
  Qdrant, vLLM, Prometheus, Caddy  Apache-2.0
  Tesseract OCR                    Apache-2.0  retrieval image, via ocrmypdf
  autossh, OpenSSH client          BSD-style   the optional tunnel container
  tusd                             MIT
  Uppy                             MIT         loaded from a CDN by the upload page
  Base images                      python:*-slim (Debian), alpine, node:*-alpine;
                                   their OS packages keep their own licenses
  Python and npm dependencies      see backend/*/requirements*.txt and
                                   frontend/webui/package-lock.json

  Model weights, downloaded on first use:
  BAAI/bge-large-en-v1.5, bge-base-en-v1.5               MIT
  sentence-transformers/allenai-specter                  Apache-2.0
  Qwen3.x checkpoints (third-party AWQ quantisations)    Apache-2.0
  openai/gpt-oss-20b                                     Apache-2.0 plus OpenAI's usage policy
  lytang/MiniCheck-Flan-T5-Large, intfloat/e5-large-v2   MIT (evaluation only)

  Evaluation datasets, downloaded by the benchmark scripts, each under the
  terms on its own dataset card: the BEIR subsets (via ir_datasets), LitSearch
  (princeton-nlp/LitSearch), RAGTruth (ParticleMedia/RAGTruth) and LitQA2
  (above). Two carry non-commercial terms, the SciFact dataset (CC BY-NC 2.0)
  and the Bespoke-MiniCheck-7B model: use them for research only.

If you publish container images built from this repository, the copyleft
components above (notably the AGPL-3.0 and GPL-3.0 ones) bring source-offer
obligations of their own.
